# EnterpriseHRSystem - API request collection
#
# Start the only host first (it serves MVC, /api/** and Swagger on one origin):
#
#   dotnet run --project src/EnterpriseHR.WebApp
#
# Contract:        docs/architecture.md  -> "API conventions"
# Scenario matrix: docs/TEST-SCENARIO-API.md
#
# Every response, success or failure, uses one envelope:
#
#   { "success": bool, "message": string, "data": object|null }
#
#   200 read/update   201 created (+ Location header)   400 validation or business rule
#   404 not found     409 conflict                      500 generic, no internals
#
# Each request is preceded by "# -> <status> <what to assert>". The expectations are
# measured against the seed fixture in db/03_seed.sql, not guessed.
#
# --- Deterministic seed ids -------------------------------------------------------
#
# The seed inserts in a fixed order, so these ids are stable across `docker compose
# down -v` + `db-init`. They are declared once here instead of being scattered through
# the requests. Ids do NOT follow EmployeeNumber order.
#
#   E004 = employee 6   Dewi Lestari, Senior Developer (position 2), 12,000,000/month,
#                       band 12,000,000-25,000,000. Target of every salary write.
#   E005 = employee 7   Rudi Hartono, IsActive = 0. Every write against it must fail.
#   E001 = employee 1   Budi Santoso, no project allocation. Target of the create case.
#   E003 = employee 5   Andi Wijaya, 30% allocated (PRJ-001).
#   E002 = employee 4   Siti Rahma, 100% allocated (PRJ-001 60% + PRJ-002 40%).
#   PRJ-001 = project 1 Active    PRJ-003 = project 3 Planning   PRJ-006 = project 6 Active
#   PRJ-004 = project 4 Completed PRJ-005 = project 5 Cancelled
#
# There is no project list endpoint yet, so project ids cannot be looked up over HTTP;
# `GET /api/projects/{{prjNNN}}/details` per seed id is the closest thing to a lookup.
# Employee ids can be resolved over HTTP - see the "Resolve seed ids" group below.

@host = http://localhost:5100

@e001 = 1
@e002 = 4
@e003 = 5
@e004 = 6
@e005 = 7

@prj001 = 1
@prj003 = 3
@prj004 = 4
@prj005 = 5
@prj006 = 6

###
### Run order and clean-up
###
# The two write groups are closed cycles, so running this file top to bottom is safe:
#
#   salary     12,000,000/pos2 -> 13,000,000/pos2 -> 30,000,000/pos3 -> 12,000,000/pos2
#   assignment create          201, one row (E001 on PRJ-006 at 40%)
#
# The assignment row cannot be removed over HTTP (no delete endpoint), and a second
# full run would turn that 201 into a 409. Between runs, drop the rows the file wrote:
#
#   DELETE FROM dbo.ProjectAssignments WHERE ProjectId = 6 AND EmployeeId = 1;
#   DELETE FROM dbo.SalaryHistories WHERE EmployeeId = 6;
#   UPDATE dbo.Employees SET Salary = 12000000.00, PositionId = 2 WHERE Id = 6;
#
# (The salary cycle restores itself; the statements above just clear the audit rows.)

###
### Resolve seed ids over HTTP
###

# -> 200 one item, employeeNumber "E004"; data.items[0].id is {{e004}}
GET {{host}}/api/employees?search=E004
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 two items, E007 and E006 (department 2 = HR)
GET {{host}}/api/employees?departmentId=2
Accept: application/json

###
### Employees - paged list (GET /api/employees)
###

# -> 200 active employees only, 9 of them; page 1, pageSize 10, totalCount 9, totalPages 1
GET {{host}}/api/employees
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 items 2, totalCount 4, totalPages 2 (IT department)
GET {{host}}/api/employees?departmentId=1&page=1&pageSize=2
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 one item, E004; search matches FullName, EmployeeNumber and Email (case-insensitive)
GET {{host}}/api/employees?search=dewi
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 items 4, page 2, totalPages 3
GET {{host}}/api/employees?page=2&pageSize=4
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 items [] with the real totalCount 9: a page past the end is empty, not an error
GET {{host}}/api/employees?page=99
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 still 9 of 9, all active: isActive is accepted by the filter but ignored by design,
#          so a client cannot widen this endpoint to soft-deleted staff
GET {{host}}/api/employees?isActive=false&pageSize=100
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 items [], totalCount 0: an unknown department is an empty page, not a 404
GET {{host}}/api/employees?departmentId=999
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 items [], totalCount 0: LIKE wildcards are escaped, so "%" is a literal search term
GET {{host}}/api/employees?search=%25
Accept: application/json

###
### Employees - list validation failures (all 400, field-error data)
###

# -> 400 data.pageSize: pageSize max is 100
GET {{host}}/api/employees?pageSize=101
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 400 data.pageSize: pageSize min is 1 (no silent clamp)
GET {{host}}/api/employees?pageSize=0
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 400 data.page: page min is 1
GET {{host}}/api/employees?page=0
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 400 data.pageSize: not an integer, model binding failure
GET {{host}}/api/employees?pageSize=abc
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 400 data.search: 256 characters, StringLength(255)
GET {{host}}/api/employees?search=aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
Accept: application/json

###
### Employee salary adjustment (PATCH /api/employees/{id}/salary)
###
# Closed cycle; every rejected request below writes nothing (no SalaryHistories row and
# no Salary change). E004 sits at the floor of the Senior Developer band, so 11,999,999
# is a 400 while the same figure would be legal for a Junior Developer.

# -> 200 message "Salary updated.", data.salary 13000000, positionId 2, positionTitle
#         "Senior Developer"; also writes SalaryHistories (12,000,000 -> 13,000,000)
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 13000000,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###

# -> 400 message "Nothing to change.", data null; same salary and same position
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 13000000,
  "newPositionId": 2,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###

# -> 400 message "New salary ... is outside the allowed range ... for position
#         'Senior Developer'."; below the band floor of 12,000,000
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 11999999,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###

# -> 400 same rule above the band ceiling of 25,000,000
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 26000000,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###

# -> 400 message "Target position not found."; checked before the band, so no write
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 30000000,
  "newPositionId": 999,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###

# -> 400 outside the Engineering Manager band (25,000,000-40,000,000): a position change
#         must also fit the new position's range
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 13000000,
  "newPositionId": 3,
  "reason": "lateral move"
}

###

# -> 200 promotion: data.salary 30000000, positionId 3, positionTitle "Engineering Manager"
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 30000000,
  "newPositionId": 3,
  "reason": "promotion"
}

###

# -> 200 restore: salary 12000000, positionId 2 again; closes the cycle for the next run
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 12000000,
  "newPositionId": 2,
  "reason": "restore seed fixture"
}

###

# -> 400 message "Cannot adjust the salary of an inactive employee." (E005, IsActive = 0)
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e005}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 8000000,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###

# -> 404 message "Employee 999 was not found.", data null
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/999/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 13000000,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###

# -> 404 message "Employee 0 was not found."; 0 matches {id:int}, unlike a non-numeric id
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/0/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 13000000,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###

# -> 404 envelope "The requested resource was not found."; "abc" never matches {id:int}
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/abc/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 13000000,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###
### Employee salary - validation and transport failures
###

# -> 400 data.reason "The Reason field is required."; model binding, no business rule ran
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 13000000
}

###

# -> 400 data.newSalary: below the decimal floor of the Range attribute
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 0,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###

# -> 400 both fields at once: data.reason and data.newSalary
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
}

###

# -> 400 data carries the JSON parser path ("$") and a "request" key, not a domain message
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 13000000,

###

# -> 415 from MVC itself, not the envelope: Content-Type must be application/json
PATCH {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: text/plain

newSalary=13000000

###
### Project details (GET /api/projects/{id}/details)
###

# -> 200 PRJ-001, Active, members 2, totalAllocationOfMembers 90
GET {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj001}}/details
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 PRJ-003, Planning, one member
GET {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj003}}/details
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 PRJ-004, Completed; a project outside Active/Planning still reads fine
GET {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj004}}/details
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 404 message "Project not found." (a thrown NotFoundException, not a bare NotFound())
GET {{host}}/api/projects/999/details
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 404 envelope "The requested resource was not found."; route constraint did not match
GET {{host}}/api/projects/abc/details
Accept: application/json

###
### Project assignment - rejected requests (none of these write a row)
###

# -> 409 message "Employee is already assigned to this project."
#         E002 is on PRJ-001 as Tech Lead (60%)
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj001}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 4,
  "roleInProject": "Developer",
  "allocationPercentage": 10
}

###

# -> 409 message "Allocation would reach 110% (current 100% + requested 10%). Maximum is
#         100%." E002 already holds 60% + 40% across two projects
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj003}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 4,
  "roleInProject": "Developer",
  "allocationPercentage": 10
}

###

# -> 400 message "Employee is not active." (E005)
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj001}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 7,
  "roleInProject": "Developer",
  "allocationPercentage": 10
}

###

# -> 400 message "Project status 'Completed' does not accept new assignments."
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj004}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 1,
  "roleInProject": "Developer",
  "allocationPercentage": 10
}

###

# -> 400 message "Project status 'Cancelled' does not accept new assignments."
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj005}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 1,
  "roleInProject": "Developer",
  "allocationPercentage": 10
}

###

# -> 404 message "Project 999 was not found."
POST {{host}}/api/projects/999/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 1,
  "roleInProject": "Developer",
  "allocationPercentage": 10
}

###

# -> 404 message "Employee 999 was not found."
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj001}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 999,
  "roleInProject": "Developer",
  "allocationPercentage": 10
}

###

# -> 400 data.allocationPercentage: Range(1, 100)
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj001}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 1,
  "roleInProject": "Developer",
  "allocationPercentage": 0
}

###

# -> 400 data.allocationPercentage: above the cap
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj001}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 1,
  "roleInProject": "Developer",
  "allocationPercentage": 101
}

###

# -> 400 data.roleInProject "The RoleInProject field is required."
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj001}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 1,
  "allocationPercentage": 10
}

###

# -> 400 data.employeeId and data.roleInProject: an empty body fails both required checks
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj001}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
}

###

# -> 400 data carries the JSON parser path ("$.employeeId") and a "request" key
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj001}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId":

###
### Project assignment - create (the only request in this file that adds a row)
###
# E001 carries no allocation yet, so 40% is within the cap. Expect a Location header of
# .../api/Projects/6/details (CreatedAtAction keeps the controller's template casing).

# -> 201 message "Created.", data { assignmentId, projectId 6, employeeId 1,
#         allocationPercentage 40 }, Location .../api/Projects/{{prj006}}/details
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj006}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 1,
  "roleInProject": "Architect",
  "allocationPercentage": 40
}

###

# -> 200 PRJ-006 with the new member listed; totalAllocationOfMembers is now 80
GET {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj006}}/details
Accept: application/json

###
### Department summary report (GET /api/reports/department-summary)
###

# -> 200 four rows ordered by department name: FIN, HR, IT, OPS.
#         IT: activeEmployeeCount 4, totalMonthlySalary 77000000, remainingBudget
#         -7000000, isOverBudget true. OPS: 0, 0, 20000000, false.
GET {{host}}/api/reports/department-summary
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 same payload: routing is case-insensitive, the lowercase template only shapes Swagger
GET {{host}}/api/Reports/Department-Summary
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 200 same payload: a trailing slash is tolerated
GET {{host}}/api/reports/department-summary/
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 404 envelope: the controller route has no action at the bare segment
GET {{host}}/api/reports
Accept: application/json

###
### Routing and method edges (middleware-level, not controller-level)
###

# -> 404 envelope "The requested resource was not found."
GET {{host}}/api/nope
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 404 envelope: there is no GET /api/employees/{id} yet
GET {{host}}/api/employees/1
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 405 envelope "The HTTP method is not supported for this resource."
DELETE {{host}}/api/employees
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 405 envelope: the report endpoint is read-only
POST {{host}}/api/reports/department-summary
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 405 envelope: the assignment endpoint is POST-only
GET {{host}}/api/projects/{{prj001}}/assign
Accept: application/json

###

# -> 405 envelope: salary is PATCH-only
PUT {{host}}/api/employees/{{e004}}/salary
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "newSalary": 13000000,
  "reason": "annual review"
}

###
### API documentation (not part of the /api contract)
###

# -> 200 Swagger UI (Development only; 404 in Production)
GET {{host}}/swagger/index.html
Accept: text/html

###

# -> 200 OpenAPI document: five paths, one per implemented endpoint
GET {{host}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
Accept: application/json
